  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an array of integers `nums` sorted in non-decreasing order (duplicates allowed), find the **starting and ending position** of a given `target`. If it isn't there, return `[-1, -1]`. Your algorithm must run in **O(log n)** time."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/157df270-2665-41d4-816e-8fb910ceb22e.svg",
      "alt": "nums is 5, 7, 7, 8, 8, 10 and the target is 8. The first index with a value of at least 8 is 3. The first index with a value of at least 9 — the first value bigger than 8 — is 5, so the last 8 is at index 4. The answer is [3, 4].",
      "width": 615,
      "height": 398,
